    <h1>Family program</h1>
    <p class="lede">Living with a loved one’s addiction affects everyone around them. The family program is education, group support, and family therapy so recovery has a chance at home instead of being quietly undone.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="wrap prose">
    <p>Family work usually begins after acute detox, when the client is stable enough for conversations that are emotionally heavy. You do not have to wait to call. Often the most useful first step is helping a family figure out what to say, and what to do if the person is not willing to come in yet.</p>
    <p>Partners, parents of adult children, adult children of parents, siblings, and sometimes close friends who are the actual support system. Calls are confidential. (866) 514-7282.</p>
  </div></section>
